From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: cut attachment-less secondaries per sample count, end
 contexts on suspend
 biblioklept

095 gave an attachment-less secondary the sample count of its first draw;
later draws with another rasterizationSamples ran with it. A secondary
cannot split the render context it inherits, so it now cuts its CS
streams where the count changes (cmd_cut_vmr_segment: flush sync
points, wait slots, end and keep the root chunks, restart the builders,
dirty all draw state). CmdExecuteCommands calls the segments in order and
splits the primary's context between them with the segment's count, so
the primary does all context work with full render-pass knowledge (the
086 failure modes: no context emission in the secondary, tile size from
cmd_select_tile_size, no overwrite of an inherited context). The cut is
taken once per API draw, outside any CS block. The primary's sync points
are flushed after the context work, before each call.

Attachment-less render passes no longer carry a render context across
suspend/resume: suspending ends it (split_render_ctx) and resuming
starts a fresh one, so the resumed pass knows its sample count.
split_render_ctx clears RESUMING so the next context is owned.

Generated-by: LLM
